{"title":"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_24\">Problem 24</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 24\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Plane\" title=\"Plane\">plane</a> contains points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a649aee592a9c37d2f9b5d5239f5e06e533130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Union\" title=\"Union\">union</a> of all disks of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the plane that cover <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. What is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/d/27d93713b2c8dc66868e447f12a3f3690fa43145.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf {(A) } 2\\pi + \\sqrt3 \\qquad \\textbf {(B) } \\frac {8\\pi}{3} \\qquad \\textbf {(C) } 3\\pi - \\frac {\\sqrt3}{2} \\qquad \\textbf {(D) } \\frac {10\\pi}{3} - \\sqrt3 \\qquad \\textbf {(E) }4\\pi - 2\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"625\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b35cef40efa03fb5dbaf36f6512271569051c0f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A=(-.5,0), B=(.5,0), C=(0,3**(.5)/2), D=(0,-3**(.5)/2);  draw(arc(A,2,-60,60),blue); draw(arc(B,2,120,240),blue); draw(circle(C,1),red);  draw(A--(.5,3^.5)); draw(B--(-.5,3^.5)); draw(A--(.5,-3^.5)); draw(B--(-.5,-3^.5)); draw(A--B);  dot(A);dot(B);dot(C);dot(D);  label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,(0,0),N); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,A/2+D/2,W); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,A/2+C/2,W); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,B/2+D/2,E); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,B/2+C/2,E); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,A/2+3D/2,W); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,A/2+3C/2,W); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,B/2+3D/2,E); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,B/2+3C/2,E);  label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,W); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,E); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,W); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,E); [/asy]\" width=\"212\" height=\"252\" /></center>\n<p>As the red circles move about segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, they cover the area we are looking for.\nOn the left side, the circle must move around pivoted on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\nOn the right side, the circle must move pivoted on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />\nHowever, at the top and bottom, the circle must lie on both A and B, giving us our upper and lower bounds.\n</p><p>This egg-like shape is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/6/736dfffedb1372a1342c41b76b561f24e133e9fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A=(-.5,0), B=(.5,0), C=(0,3**(.5)/2), D=(0,-3**(.5)/2);  draw(arc(A,2,-60,60),blue); draw(arc(B,2,120,240),blue); draw(arc(C,1,60,120),red); draw(arc(D,1,-120,-60),red);  draw(A--(.5,3^.5)); draw(B--(-.5,3^.5)); draw(A--(.5,-3^.5)); draw(B--(-.5,-3^.5)); draw(A--B);  dot(A);dot(B);dot(C);dot(D); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,W); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,E); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,W); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,E);  label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,(0,0),N); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,A/2+D/2,W); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,A/2+C/2,W); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,B/2+D/2,E); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,B/2+C/2,E); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,A/2+3D/2,W); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,A/2+3C/2,W); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,B/2+3D/2,E); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,B/2+3C/2,E); [/asy]\" width=\"202\" height=\"252\" /></center>\n<p>The area of the region can be found by dividing it into several sectors, namely\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/807594c4f0b1dc1e4a857cabc341db3b94386c71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} A &amp;= 2(\\mathrm{Blue\\ Sector}) + 2(\\mathrm{Red\\ Sector}) - 2(\\mathrm{Equilateral\\ Triangle}) \\\\ A &amp;= 2\\left(\\frac{120^\\circ}{360^\\circ} \\cdot \\pi (2)^2\\right) + 2\\left(\\frac{60^\\circ}{360^\\circ} \\cdot \\pi (1)^2\\right) - 2\\left(\\frac{(1)^2\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\right) \\\\ A &amp;= \\frac{8\\pi}{3} + \\frac{\\pi}{3} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ A &amp;= 3\\pi - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\Longrightarrow \\textbf {(C)}\\end{align*}\" width=\"486\" height=\"175\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A\">2004 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Pr